{"duration_api_ms":120179,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"11822100-52a0-4ff4-8f77-31c392ad7d0b","total_cost_usd":0.6297782000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":125638,"cache_read_input_tokens":138991,"output_tokens":9942,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5507},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":125638,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4371,"cache_read_input_tokens":129451,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5727},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":9942,"cacheReadInputTokens":138991,"cacheCreationInputTokens":125638,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6297782000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":5507,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"single-gateway\",\"requirement\":\"node3 has a single gateway address for reaching node4\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3's route table shows a single static route to 10.10.14.0/24 via the VRRP virtual IP 10.10.13.254 on eth1, and ping from node3 to node4 (10.10.14.4) succeeds using this one gateway address, both before and after the failover/failback cycle and after all node restarts.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-55888e385e22430c\",\"cmd-852ee6fd266b428d\",\"cmd-c298522b3f2c4b52\",\"cmd-60f4b62c5a824353\",\"cmd-2517a605a7184d33\"]},{\"id\":\"gateway-available-router-down\",\"requirement\":\"Gateway stays available when either router (node1 or node2) is down\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"With node1's transit interfaces disabled, node2 (VRRP backup, priority 100) promoted to MASTER on both VRRP groups within seconds and node3->node4 ping continued through the same gateway IP; the continuous ping log showed only 2/34 probes lost during the whole failover+failback window. The reverse case (node2 down while node1 healthy) is not separately exercised, but is the normal/no-failover state since node1 is preferred master, so no additional risk is implied.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-22f51c72e8ae4ffe\",\"cmd-f722d07eece341e0\",\"cmd-34d4d378028f4b30\",\"cmd-d9b8ab7fcec94d91\"]},{\"id\":\"prefer-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Gateway prefers node1 while node1 is healthy (including automatic failback)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 was configured with VRRP priority 150 vs node2's 100 with preempt enabled (default). After re-enabling node1's interfaces post-failover, node1 automatically reclaimed MASTER on both VRRP groups within seconds and node2 returned to BACKUP, confirmed again after all node restarts (node1 MASTER, node2 BACKUP).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-54113b3ad1c34b01\",\"cmd-91a195750d60428c\",\"cmd-e4253b3bf4914910\",\"cmd-c5bb530f264f41ef\",\"cmd-3af666383b45408a\"]},{\"id\":\"ansible-implementation\",\"requirement\":\"Solution implemented using Ansible\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A working ansible-playbook (site.yml) run from control node node5 configured the interface addresses and VRRP groups on node1/node2 (via an Ansible shell task pushing VyOS config commands, after the vyos.vyos resource modules failed against this VyOS build) and the RHEL7 interface/route files on node3/node4 (via Ansible raw module, since RHEL7's Python 2.7 is incompatible with this ansible-core). Some manual out-of-band VyOS commands were run on node1 during troubleshooting before the playbook succeeded, but the final ansible-playbook run applied the complete, idempotent configuration (addresses + VRRP groups) to both routers.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8339af8677924e2a\",\"cmd-844e89abdea049e0\",\"cmd-d97fe1f55d7b4ee0\",\"cmd-4a3d53de33c54664\",\"cmd-fbf3a69519a944db\",\"cmd-747107e255804f0f\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node1\",\"requirement\":\"node1 node-restart evidence: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 32669db3 with VRRP MASTER captured, reboot acknowledged, new boot_id ea4bdbd8 confirms restart, and post-restart interfaces/VIPs, VRRP MASTER role, and node3->node4 ping confirm full recovery.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-55a7a229378a40db\",\"cmd-1acd3e74f5b44488\",\"cmd-c9b05a9c469943f8\",\"cmd-de5052f59e5b4b7d\",\"cmd-64e0c5f3a8124118\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node2\",\"requirement\":\"node2 node-restart evidence: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 9d3cb897 with VRRP BACKUP captured, reboot acknowledged, new boot_id 94a4b677 confirms restart, and post-restart interfaces and VRRP BACKUP role confirm recovery; node1 remained unaffected master throughout.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a46c32349b234732\",\"cmd-e2e96624984143f4\",\"cmd-bc587d7a30f2459c\",\"cmd-01660a2ea83f4c80\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node3\",\"requirement\":\"node3 node-restart evidence: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 73bafeef captured, reboot acknowledged (after correcting an initial 'must be root' sudo issue), new boot_id 57fbb60c confirms restart, and post-restart ifcfg-eth1 and successful ping to node4 confirm recovery of both interface config and data-plane connectivity.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-1606a2a36b1a47ee\",\"cmd-0a2f0e3c45ab43ef\",\"cmd-2d9eb50442f447f0\",\"cmd-60f4b62c5a824353\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node4\",\"requirement\":\"node4 node-restart evidence: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id ef457a88 captured, reboot acknowledged, new boot_id 8cd601a8 confirms restart, and post-restart interface/route and successful ping to node3 confirm recovery.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3cfefb8e5d6e4a18\",\"cmd-69fb311443874dfb\",\"cmd-11c68337dfd94112\",\"cmd-f8d4f34d7f564bdf\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node5\",\"requirement\":\"node5 (Ansible control node) node-restart evidence: baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"status\":\"partially_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id eefaca89 captured, reboot acknowledged, new boot_id d7b5d099 confirms restart, and the ansible-vrrp project files persisted. However, post-restart SSH from node5 to node1/node2 as the vyos user failed with 'Permission denied' because the manually appended public key in /home/vyos/.ssh/authorized_keys on the VyOS nodes did not persist (VyOS only persists /config), which the executor itself flagged as a limitation. This means the Ansible control path to the routers was not fully re-verified as functional post-restart, even though direct managed-node access to node1/node2 (outside the node5 SSH path) still worked.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-79617e0c156b4342\",\"cmd-21e1ad798b6f4889\",\"cmd-b73feac27a56476f\",\"cmd-0d24d9b756c84558\"]},{\"id\":\"overall-cluster-health\",\"requirement\":\"Overall cluster/service health after all restarts\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"After all five nodes were sequentially restarted, node1 is MASTER (priority 150) on both VRRP groups, node2 is BACKUP (priority 100), and node4->node3 ping succeeds through the persisted single gateway, demonstrating the solution survives a full cluster restart cycle.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c5bb530f264f41ef\",\"cmd-3af666383b45408a\",\"cmd-eaf0fc68d3fd4590\"]}],\"confidence\":0.85,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.7,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands map clearly to discovery, implementation, or bounded/restored testin
